Requirement 1 – Document Checklist Display Area

The existing Document Checklist functionality is already implemented in the application.

The requirement is to improve the way the available space is used when adding multiple documents.

Expected Behavior

When the user clicks Add and continues adding documents:

- The available space inside the existing Document Checklist window should be utilized properly.
- The document adding/list area should continue using the available space until it reaches the existing footer area.
- The existing Total + Save footer section must remain visible.
- The Save button must not be pushed outside, hidden, or covered when additional documents are added.
- The existing Total row must remain in the footer section exactly as it is currently displayed.
- The existing footer styling and appearance should remain unchanged.
- A scrollbar should not appear prematurely while there is still available space for displaying additional documents.
- Once the document content reaches/exceeds the available area, scrolling should be allowed so the user can continue working with the documents.
- Even after scrolling becomes necessary, the existing Total + Save footer must remain visible/accessibile.

Important

This is an existing legacy Angular + PrimeNG application using SCSS.

The Document Checklist, modal/window, footer, Total row, Save button, document rows, and existing styling are already implemented.

Do not create or redesign the Document Checklist.

Before making changes, inspect the existing:

- Angular component/controller implementation
- HTML/template
- SCSS
- PrimeNG dialog/modal configuration
- Existing Document Checklist layout and DOM structure

Based on the existing implementation, determine the minimum required change to achieve the expected behavior above.

Do not prescribe a new layout or architecture.

Do not unnecessarily modify the existing HTML/SCSS/component logic.

Do not change:

- Existing footer design
- Total row styling
- Save button behavior
- Document adding functionality
- Document row design
- Existing PrimeNG configuration unless required
- Any unrelated functionality

Do not refactor unrelated legacy code.

Acceptance Criteria

1. Existing Document Checklist opens and looks the same.
2. User can continue adding documents while available space exists.
3. Save button remains visible while documents are being added.
4. Total row remains in the existing footer section.
5. Footer does not get pushed outside the visible window.
6. No scrollbar appears while sufficient space is still available.
7. When the available document area is exhausted, scrolling becomes available.
8. Footer remains visible/accessibile when scrolling is required.
9. Existing CSS/SCSS styling remains visually unchanged.
10. No unrelated functionality is affected.

Important: Inspect the existing legacy implementation first and decide the appropriate Angular/SCSS/PrimeNG change yourself. Only make the minimum changes necessary to satisfy this requirement.
